---
description: Cursor Rule Editing Workaround
globs: "**/*.mdc-tmp,**/*.mdc"
alwaysApply: false
---
# Cursor Rule Editing Workaround

Standards for creating and editing cursor rule files to work around Cursor limitations.

<rule>
name: cursor_rule_editing_workaround
description: Enforces the workaround process for editing cursor rule files
filters:
  # Match any .mdc or .mdc-tmp files
  - type: file_extension
    pattern: "\\.mdc(-tmp)?$"
  # Match file creation and modification events
  - type: event
    pattern: "(file_create|file_modify)"

actions:
  - type: suggest
    message: |
      ## Cursor Rule Editing Workaround Process

      Due to Cursor limitations, follow this process when editing rule files:

      ### 1. Temporary File Creation
      - Use `.mdc-tmp` extension for all new or modified cursor rules
      - Place temporary files in same location as target `.mdc` file

      ### 2. Process for Modifying Existing Rules
      - Copy existing `.mdc` file to `.mdc-tmp` before ANY modifications
      - Get user approval of the initial copy
      - Only after approval, make edits in the temporary file
      - Maintain original file until changes are approved

      ### 3. File Finalization
      - Review changes in temporary file
      - Use terminal command (`cp` or `mv`) to create final `.mdc` file - NEVER use internal file editing tools
      - Remove temporary file after successful creation

      Due to known Cursor limitations, internal file editing tools cannot be used to create or modify `.mdc` files directly.
      Always use terminal commands like `cp` or `mv` for the final step.

examples:
  - input: |
      # Creating new rule:
      touch cursor/rules/example-rule.mdc-tmp
      # Edit temporary file...
      cp cursor/rules/example-rule.mdc-tmp cursor/rules/example-rule.mdc
      rm cursor/rules/example-rule.mdc-tmp

      # Modifying existing rule:
      cp cursor/rules/existing-rule.mdc cursor/rules/existing-rule.mdc-tmp
      # Edit temporary file...
      cp cursor/rules/existing-rule.mdc-tmp cursor/rules/existing-rule.mdc
      rm cursor/rules/existing-rule.mdc-tmp
    output: "Following the proper rule editing workaround process"

metadata:
  priority: high
  version: 1.0
  ref: https://github.com/getcursor/cursor/issues/2683
</rule> 